        ":question/id": "47951087-d6bf-5e9e-b681-ee4e24b433d0",
        ":question/problem": "Let $u = \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $v = \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$. Given that $u\u22a5v$ and $x > 0$, find the value of $x$.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $u\u22a5v$ ($u$ and $v$ are perpendicular) if and only if $u\\cdot v=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v &={u}_{x}\\cdot {v}_{x}+{u}_{y}\\cdot {v}_{y} \\\\  &=x\\cdot x+(-2)\\cdot 2 \\\\  &={x}^{2}-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v &=0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4 &=0 \\\\ {x}^{2} &=4 \\\\ x &=\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the negative solution since we are told that $x>0.$ Therefore, $x=2.$",
