        ":question/id": "ddd184d7-f9a1-58c1-977c-bb851aecf877",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of $x$ given that $a = \u27e8x,-6x, 3\u27e9, b = \u27e8x, 1, 3\u27e9$ and $a\u22a5b$?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $a\u22a5b$ ($a$ and $b$ are perpendicular) if and only if $a\\cdot b=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b &={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  &=x\\cdot x+(-6x)\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 3 \\\\  &={x}^{2}-6x+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b &=0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-6x+9 &=0 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} &=0 \\\\ x-3 &=0 \\\\ x &=3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
